course: dictionary
lesson: 13915
title: Lazily
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word lazily is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. Add -ly to lazy and you get lazily: «He lazily picked up a pen.» The word tells us how he picked it up: without much effort, as if he could not be bothered.
explain: Lazily can also describe a slow, gentle movement that feels calm: «The river flowed lazily past the boats.» Nothing is rushing here. Ask yourself: is the action slow and relaxed, or is someone just not trying? The other words in the sentence will tell you which.
explain: Writers use lazily to paint warm, sleepy summer scenes: «The cat stretched lazily in the sun.» It can also criticise someone who is not trying hard: «He lazily left his homework until the last minute.» Look at the words around it to find out whether the feeling is peaceful or cross.
fact: Lazily is an adverb: it tells you how an action happens.
fact: «Lazily» means in a lazy way, without effort or energy.
fact: «Lazily» can also mean slowly and gently, in a relaxed way.
fact: The comparative form is more lazily, and the superlative form is most lazily.
fact: Lazily comes from the adjective lazy, with -ly added to the end.
exercise: «The dog lazily wagged its tail in the warm sun.» How does the dog wag its tail? | Very loudly | With great speed and energy | Angrily | *In a slow, relaxed way
exercise: «Rat and Mole lay lazily in the boat all afternoon.» What does lazily tell us? | *Relaxed and calm, without any hurry | Fast and noisy | Frightened and alone
exercise: «Sam lazily left his bag on the floor and never tidied his room.» What does lazily suggest about Sam? | He is very excited | He is lost | He is cold and wet | *He is not trying hard
test: «The river flowed lazily past the sleepy village.» What does lazily mean here? | *Slowly and gently | Very fast and dangerous | Without a single drop of water | In a noisy way
test: «The cat lazily stretched out on the warm wall.» Which word tells us how the cat stretched? | warm | wall | cat | *lazily
exam: «Lily lazily sorted her toys, and her mum had to ask three times.» What does lazily suggest? | Lily is cold and wet | *Lily is slow and not trying hard | Lily is lost in the park | Lily is very happy and excited
